Hmm wait — careful: `jsonEncode(ledger.toJson())` contains byModel keys like "model-a"... `contains('"model"')` would match `"model-a"`? No: `"model-a"` — the substring `"model` yes but `"model"` requires closing quote right after. byModel key serializes as `"model-a":{...}` — the substring `"model"` is not present. OK good. But `byModel` maps with key exactly `model`? assistantLine default model is 'model-a', not 'model'. Fine. Actually let me use a cleaner assertion: `jsonEncode(ledger.toJson())` does not contain `'"model":'`. Keys in json: byModel map keys would produce `"model-a":`. And the segment-level field WOULD be `"model":`. So `isNot(contains('"model":'))` works.

